From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: fix Linux 6.6 FORTIFY strict-flex-arrays traps and sta.c syntax typo

Convert trailing zero-length arrays [0] to C99 flexible array members [] in
non-embedded structs across dot11r_ft.h, dot11w_pmf.h, dot11i_wpa.h, oid.h,
rrm_cmm.h, qos.h, mlme.h, and wapp_cmm_type.h so Linux 6.6 CONFIG_FORTIFY_SOURCE
computes true allocation bounds rather than 0 bytes under -fstrict-flex-arrays=3.

Replace HEADER_802_11.Octet[0] pointer accesses in cmm_tkip.c and pmf.c with
(UCHAR *)(pHdr + 1) / (UCHAR *)(pFrame + 1), pass $(call cc-option,-fstrict-flex-arrays=0)
in mt_wifi_ap/Makefile for the remaining wire/firmware ABI [1] structs
(EID_STRUCT, FRAME_802_11, NDIS_*_KEY), and fix the stray "t" token on the
MTWF_DBG format string literal in sta/sta.c:662.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
